  "reviewed_observations": [
    "The four-epoch autoencoder was materially under-optimized. By 64 to 256 epochs, reconstruction loss fell sharply and most apparent local-geometry fragility recovered, so the earlier short-horizon degradation is partly an optimization artifact rather than clean representation-class evidence.",
    "Well-optimized autoencoders and PCA preserve different controlled geometry. PCA better preserves observed-space pairwise ordering, while converged autoencoders can better preserve the known synthetic latent reference pairwise geometry. There is no universal winner.",
    "The ordered lag-1 predictive autoencoder beat the within-sequence shuffled-successor null on every declared geometry metric at every noise level, with every recorded minimum seed-level effect still positive. Temporal correspondence therefore materially constrains the learned predictive representation in this synthetic system.",
    "The ordered lag-1 predictive autoencoder did not establish superiority over the matched-capacity reconstruction autoencoder. Effects are small or mixed at low to moderate noise, and local geometry becomes modestly worse for prediction at high noise.",
    "Objective-specific training losses are diagnostics only and are not cross-objective scores.",
    "No T-PHATE or external temporal-SSL efficacy result is contained in this evidence.",
    "All reference geometry is synthetic, not biological ground truth, neural decoding performance, BCI learnability, or clinical evidence."
  ],
